meta {
  name: AI Block Window Recommendation
  type: http
  seq: 8
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/railways/block-windows/recommendation/
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "task_id": "TMS-190",
    "date": "2026-09-07"
  }
}

vars:pre-request {
  baseUrl: http://127.0.0.1:8000/
}

assert {
  res.status: in [200, 400]
}

docs {
  # Unified AI Block Window Recommendation & Rescheduling

  Single endpoint that merges slot discovery, conflict checks, and 1-click slot updates.

  The Railway-AI risk scorer and CP-SAT optimizer run inside this Django
  backend. No separate ML service URL or second deployment is required.
  When the embedded optimizer is unavailable, the response falls back to the
  deterministic timetable-gap planner. Inspect each returned window's
  `algorithm` field to identify which planner produced it.

  ## Mode 1: Pre-Creation Slot Discovery
  Find optimal collision-free slots before creating any BlockWindow:
  ```json
  {
    "task_id": "TMS-696",
    "date": "2026-09-08"
  }
  ```
  
  ## Mode 2: Continuous Conflict Check & Recommendation for Existing Block
  Evaluate train conflicts and suggest better slots for an existing block window:
  ```json
  {
    "block_window_id": 1,
    "task_id": "TMS-696"
  }
  ```
  *(Can also be called via GET: `{{baseUrl}}/railways/block-windows/recommendation/?block_window_id=1&task_id=TMS-696`)*
  
  ## Mode 3: 1-Click Auto-Apply AI Recommendation
  Automatically apply the AI-recommended slot to the BlockWindow in the database:
  ```json
  {
    "block_window_id": 1,
    "task_id": "TMS-696",
    "apply": true
  }
  ```

  A successful embedded-AI result uses:
  ```json
  { "algorithm": "Embedded Railway-AI CP-SAT" }
  ```
}
